M game-dev "Game Dev action log reads gamedev_receipts_command so bot and UI actions share durable results. Screen reports use POST /api/ui/app-state app=game-dev and appear through neyvia.gamedev.state; reported selection never establishes native engine success." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"bridges","data":"Native bridges use the literal loopback port in the selected project capability configuration, excluding public port 47881. Unity batchmode/nographics, Godot --headless --editor, and Blender --background preserve the actual native scene operations. A pending request is not a completed edit; use the same requestId and reread inspect after success.","key":"10","section":"guidance"}
M game-dev "Native bridges use the literal loopback port in the selected project capability configuration, excluding public port 47881. Unity batchmode/nographics, Godot --headless --editor, and Blender --background preserve the actual native scene operations. A pending request is not a completed edit; use the same requestId and reread inspect after success." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"bridges","data":"Observe sessions with explicit engine, projectPath and context before action. CL fills sessionId only when this current observation contains one exact native session; it never guesses a native session from the chat identity.","key":"11","section":"guidance"}
M game-dev "Observe sessions with explicit engine, projectPath and context before action. CL fills sessionId only when this current observation contains one exact native session; it never guesses a native session from the chat identity." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"bridges","data":"Unity, Godot and Blender register with a stable per-instance clientId. Identical retry replies preserve the native session; changed affinity or capabilities refuse reuse. Separate editor instances keep separate identities, so CL still refuses ambiguous session selection. Unity idle polls never execute empty nested request objects.","key":"12","section":"guidance"}
M game-dev "Unity, Godot and Blender register with a stable per-instance clientId. Identical retry replies preserve the native session; changed affinity or capabilities refuse reuse. Separate editor instances keep separate identities, so CL still refuses ambiguous session selection. Unity idle polls never execute empty nested request objects." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"bridges","data":"LAYA3D uses the shared scene.transcribe, laya.judge and scene.improve core. Read manuals/cl/laya-3d.cl for defect predicates and manuals/cl/laya-3d-image.cl for image-model acceptance. Blender transcribe observes mesh facts; canonical renders fixed front/side/back/top views; snapshot/restore guard named mesh_fix operations. shape_program executes literal bounded shape operations in its own collection, not Python code.","key":"13","section":"guidance"}
M game-dev "LAYA3D uses the shared scene.transcribe, laya.judge and scene.improve core. Read manuals/cl/laya-3d.cl for defect predicates and manuals/cl/laya-3d-image.cl for image-model acceptance. Blender transcribe observes mesh facts; canonical renders fixed front/side/back/top views; snapshot/restore guard named mesh_fix operations. shape_program executes literal bounded shape operations in its own collection, not Python code." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"bridges","data":"For image input call scene.improve with domain=laya3d, source={sessionId, sheet, spec:{object, cells:[{cell, caption, role, camera:{yaw, elevation, roll}, illustrationOnly?}]}} and budget={max_steps:1,max_seconds:240,allowed_fixes:[shape.refit],guards:{outline_iou_mean:min}}; call it once per program edit until the ladder is exhausted. Cells are physical row-major positions from detected gutters, never printed numbers. Camera readings may list alternatives and are fitted within 25 degrees; the first cell is the anchor. Illustration-only cells (topology guides, exploded, detail) are recorded, never geometry. The returned modelPath resumes the CL model; scene.transcribe with sessionId/modelPath observes the live model without rebuilding. Predicates read the shape-model node (worst and mean view outline IoU, colour and extent bands); per-view numbers are evidence. Silhouettes cannot recover concavities; held-out views measure 3D shape.","key":"14","section":"guidance"}
M game-dev "For image input call scene.improve with domain=laya3d, source={sessionId, sheet, spec:{object, cells:[{cell, caption, role, camera:{yaw, elevation, roll}, illustrationOnly?}]}} and budget={max_steps:1,max_seconds:240,allowed_fixes:[shape.refit],guards:{outline_iou_mean:min}}; call it once per program edit until the ladder is exhausted. Cells are physical row-major positions from detected gutters, never printed numbers. Camera readings may list alternatives and are fitted within 25 degrees; the first cell is the anchor. Illustration-only cells (topology guides, exploded, detail) are recorded, never geometry. The returned modelPath resumes the CL model; scene.transcribe with sessionId/modelPath observes the live model without rebuilding. Predicates read the shape-model node (worst and mean view outline IoU, colour and extent bands); per-view numbers are evidence. Silhouettes cannot recover concavities; held-out views measure 3D shape." src:"authored manual" state:verified
-- @record {"chapter":"bridges","data":"Godot and Unity transcribe expose live native hierarchy, scale, mesh/material/reference facts and collider intent to the same predicates; engine.scale is the only automatic engine fix, collider and reference findings stay review-only. Godot's client reconnects with the same clientId when the editor's first scan outlasts the socket handshake. A Unity project needs ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt, or UPM adds and downloads the default template packages; the bridge package declares its JSON, UnityWebRequest and Physics modules. Blender scene.improve callers pass guards {silhouette_quality:min}; transcribe keeps render paths out of the Scene so rollback is checked by sha256. Roblox observer is code-only until an installed Studio session is available. Native texture upscale is bounded resampling, not invented detail; topology flow and rendered lighting remain review-only when not measured.","key":"15","section":"guidance"}
M game-dev "Godot and Unity transcribe expose live native hierarchy, scale, mesh/material/reference facts and collider intent to the same predicates; engine.scale is the only automatic engine fix, collider and reference findings stay review-only. Godot's client reconnects with the same clientId when the editor's first scan outlasts the socket handshake. A Unity project needs ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt, or UPM adds and downloads the default template packages; the bridge package declares its JSON, UnityWebRequest and Physics modules. Blender scene.improve callers pass guards {silhouette_quality:min}; transcribe keeps render paths out of the Scene so rollback is checked by sha256. Roblox observer is code-only until an installed Studio session is available. Native texture upscale is bounded resampling, not invented detail; topology flow and rendered lighting remain review-only when not measured." src:"authored manual" state:verified
